{"step_index":95,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T01:29:08Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-10-26T01:28:58Z sender=747a770e-7572-4f05-a822-16192dccccd8 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=# ART Runtime Inspection: GC, Heap Profiling, Lock Contention & Jank Monitoring\n\nInspected repository: `/home/ethen/workspace/voyah/projects/8397/code/qssi/art` (shallow commit `9a380e42`, Android 15 / V QSSI tree). All paths below are relative to `/home/ethen/workspace/voyah/projects/8397/code/qssi/art/` unless an absolute path is noted.\n\n---\n\n## 1. GC, Heap, Blocking Allocations & OOME Diagnostics\n\n### 1.1 Slow GC & Long Pause Detection Thresholds and Logging\n* **Default Constants** (`runtime/gc/heap.h:146-149`, `runtime/gc/heap.cc:199, 229`):\n  * `kDefaultLongPauseLogThreshold = MsToNs(5)` (**5 ms**; `long_pause_log_threshold_`, `heap.h:1407`, `heap.cc:329`).\n  * `kDefaultLongPauseLogThresholdGcStress = MsToNs(50)` (**50 ms**).\n  * `kDefaultLongGCLogThreshold = MsToNs(100)` (**100 ms**; `long_gc_log_threshold_`, `heap.h:1410`, `heap.cc:330`).\n  * `kDefaultLongGCLogThresholdGcStress = MsToNs(1000)` (**1000 ms**).\n  * `kGcStressModeGcLogSampleFrequencyNs = MsToNs(10 * 1000)` (**10 s** rate-limit in `gcstress`).\n  * `kLogAllGCs = false` (`heap.cc:199`).\n* **Runtime Options** (`runtime/runtime_options.def:71-74, 83`, `runtime/parsed_options.cc:222-227, 238-242, 802-803`, `runtime/runtime.cc:1851-1854`):\n  * `-XX:LongPauseLogThreshold=<ms>` (`Opt::LongPauseLogThreshold`, converted via `MsToNs`).\n  * `-XX:LongGCLogThreshold=<ms>` (`Opt::LongGCLogThreshold`, converted via `MsToNs`).\n  * `-XX:AlwaysLogExplicitGcs:<bool>` (`Opt::AlwaysLogExplicitGcs`, default `true`, `always_log_explicit_gcs_`, `heap.h:1430`).\n  * Note: `AndroidRuntime.cpp` (`frameworks/base/core/jni/AndroidRuntime.cpp:829, 1042`) passes `-verbose:gc` by default and only overrides `-XX:LongPauseLogThreshold` / `-XX:LongGCLogThreshold` if supplied via `dalvik.vm.extra-opts`.\n* **Slow GC Log Trigger (`Heap::LogGC`)** (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:2968-3012`):\n  * Checks `CareAboutPauseTimes()` (`heap.cc:231-233`), which returns `Runtime::Current()->InJankPerceptibleProcessState()` (foreground / perceptible app states).\n  * Emits `LOG(INFO)` to logcat when:\n    1. `kLogAllGCs` is true, OR\n    2. `gc_cause == kGcCauseExplicit && always_log_explicit_gcs_`, OR\n    3. `CareAboutPauseTimes()` is true AND (`duration > long_gc_log_threshold_` [100 ms] OR `(gc_cause == kGcCauseForAlloc && duration > long_pause_log_threshold_)` [5 ms] OR any stop-the-world pause in `GetCurrentGcIteration()->GetPauseTimes()` is `>= long_pause_log_threshold_` [5 ms]).\n  * Logcat format (`heap.cc:3001-3009`):\n    `<GcCause> <CollectorName> GC freed <alloc_freed> AllocSpace bytes, <los_objs>(<los_bytes>) LOS objects, <pct>% free, <allocated>/<footprint>, paused <p1,p2,...> total <duration>`\n  * If `-verbose:heap` (`VLOG(heap)`) is active, also dumps full `TimingLogger` phase breakdown (`heap.cc:3010`).\n* **Additional `long_pause_log_threshold_` (5 ms) Jank Warnings in `Heap`**:\n  * `Heap::WaitForGcToCompleteLocked(GcCause, Thread*)` (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:3713-3751`): if `wait_time > long_pause_log_threshold_`, logs `LOG(INFO) << \"WaitForGcToComplete blocked \" << cause << \" on \" << last_gc_cause << \" for \" << PrettyDuration(wait_time)` (`L3738-3741`).\n  * `Heap::IncrementDisableThreadFlip(Thread*)` (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:1019-1049`): JNI critical region entry waiting on GC thread flip; logs `LOG(INFO) << \"IncrementDisableThreadFlip blocked for \" << PrettyDuration(wait_time)` if `wait_time > long_pause_log_threshold_` (`L1045-1047`).\n  * `Heap::ThreadFlipBegin(Thread*)` (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:1084-1107`): GC waiting on active JNI critical regions; logs `LOG(INFO) << \"ThreadFlipBegin blocked for \" << PrettyDuration(wait_time)` if `wait_time > long_pause_log_threshold_` (`L1103-1105`).\n\n### 1.2 GC Pause, Throughput & Rate Histograms and `ArtMetrics`\n* **Heap GC Rate Histograms** (`runtime/gc/heap.h:1744-1760`, `runtime/gc/heap.cc:422-429, 1294-1357, 1413-1425, 3020-3079`):\n  * Window: `kGcCountRateHistogramWindowDuration = MsToNs(10 * 1000)` (**10 s**), `kGcCountRateMaxBucketCount = 200`, `kGcCountRateHistogramMaxNumMissedWindows = 100`.\n  * `gc_count_rate_histogram_` (`\"gc count rate histogram\"`) & `blocking_gc_count_rate_histogram_` (`\"blocking gc count rate histogram\"`), updated in `Heap::FinishGC` -> `Heap::UpdateGcCountRateHistograms()` (`heap.cc:3014-3079`).\n  * Exposed via `Heap::DumpGcCountRateHistogram` / `DumpBlockingGcCountRateHistogram` (`heap.cc:1413-1425`, backing `Debug.getRuntimeStat(\"art.gc.gc-count-rate-histogram\")` and `\"art.gc.blocking-gc-count-rate-histogram\"`), `SIGQUIT` ANR traces (`Heap::DumpForSigQuit` -> `DumpGcPerformanceInfo`, `heap.cc:1294-1357, 3753-3766`), and shutdown (`-XX:DumpGCPerformanceOnShutdown`).\n* **Per-Collector Histograms** (`runtime/gc/collector/garbage_collector.h:170-200`, `garbage_collector.cc:115-139, 145-195, 497-548`):\n  * `pause_histogram_` (`\"<name> paused\"`, bucket width `500` us, `32` buckets).\n  * `rss_histogram_` (`\"<name> peak-rss\"`, bucket width `10` KB, `16` buckets, sampled via `mincore()` in `ExtractRssFromMincore`, `L145-195` when `-Xgc:measure` is enabled).\n  * `freed_bytes_histogram_` (`\"<name> freed-bytes\"`, bucket width `10` KB, `16` buckets).\n  * `ConcurrentCopying::rb_slow_path_time_histogram_` (`runtime/gc/collector/concurrent_copying.h:467-470`, `concurrent_copying.cc:110-111, 3738-3744, 3811-3822`): `\"Mutator time in read barrier slow path\"` (bucket `500`, `32` buckets) + `rb_slow_path_count_total_` / `rb_slow_path_count_gc_total_`.\n* **ART Telemetry (`ArtMetrics` -> statsd / logcat / file)** (`garbage_collector.cc:243-279`, `mark_compact.cc:465-468, 577-580`, `concurrent_copying.cc:146-165`, `libartbase/base/flags.h:266-317`):\n  * Records `WorldStopTimeDuringGCAvg`, `GcWorldStopTime[Delta]`, `GcWorldStopCount[Delta]`, `TotalGcCollectionTime[Delta]`, and Young/Full per-collector metrics: `CollectionTime` histogram, `Count[Delta]`, `TracingThroughput[Avg]` (scanned MB/s), `Throughput[Avg]` (freed MB/CPU-s via `Iteration::GetEstimatedThroughput`, `garbage_collector.cc:110-113`), `ScannedBytes[Delta]`, `FreedBytes[Delta]`, `Duration[Delta]`, and `AppSlowPathDurationDelta`.\n  * Controlled via `Flags` (`libartbase/base/flags.h:266-317`): `persist.device_config.runtime_native.metrics.*` / `dalvik.vm.metrics.*` (default 2% session sampling to statsd: `MetricsReportingMods=2`, `MetricsReportingNumMods=100`, `MetricsWriteToStatsd=true`).\n\n### 1.3 ATrace / Systrace Markers in GC (`ATRP` / `ATRACE_TAG_DALVIK`)\n* **Automatic Phase Tracing via `TimingLogger::ScopedTiming`** (`runtime/base/timing_logger.h:182-198`, `runtime/base/timing_logger.cc:139-148`):\n  * Every `TimingLogger::StartTiming(label)` calls `ATraceBegin(label)` (`L142`) and `EndTiming()` calls `ATraceEnd()` (`L147`). Thus **every** GC phase wrapped in `TimingLogger::ScopedTiming` in `MarkCompact` (`mark_compact.cc:672, 790, 1190, 1514-1664, 3362, 3680, 4189, 4234, 4392, ...`, e.g., `(Paused)MarkingPause`, `ReclaimPhase`, `(Paused)KernelPreparation`, `CompactionPhase`) and `ConcurrentCopying` (`concurrent_copying.cc:249, 404, 542-579, 754, 804, 844, 1371, 1444, 2487, 2638, ...`, e.g., `InitializePhase`, `(Paused)FlipCallback`, `FlipThreadRoots`, `MarkingPhase`, `CopyingPhase`, `ReclaimPhase`) automatically appears as a nested ATrace/Perfetto slice.\n* **Explicit Collector & Heap Slices and Counters**:\n  * `GarbageCollector::Run` (`garbage_collector.cc:47-84, 198, 281-285`): outer `ScopedTrace(\"<PrettyCause> <CollectorName> GC\")` (`L198`) and `TraceGCMetric` counters (`ATraceIntegerValue` with int32 wrap protection): `\"freed_normal_object_bytes\"`, `\"freed_large_object_bytes\"`, `\"freed_bytes\"`.\n  * `MarkCompact::RunPhases` -> `TraceFaults()` (`mark_compact.cc:858-870, 881, 888`): reads `getrusage(RUSAGE_THREAD)` and emits `ATraceIntegerValue(\"Minflt-GC\", usage.ru_minflt)` and `ATraceIntegerValue(\"Majflt-GC\", usage.ru_majflt)` (major faults = disk/zram decompression during GC).\n  * `ConcurrentCopying::MarkFromReadBarrierWithMeasurements` (`concurrent_copying.cc:3797`): `ScopedTrace` on read-barrier slow path when `-Xgc:measure` is active.\n  * `Heap::TraceHeapSize(size_t)` (`heap.cc:2745-2747, 3824, 4882`): emits `ATraceIntegerValue(\"Heap size (KB)\", heap_size / KB)` after GC utilization sizing and on TLAB/bulk allocations (`>= 16 KB`).\n  * `Heap` blocking/trim/trigger slices (`heap.cc`): `\"IncrementDisableThreadFlip\"` (`L1035`), `\"Deflating monitors\"` (`L1624`), `Heap::TrimIndirectReferenceTables` (`L1656`), `Heap::TrimSpaces` (`L1722`), `\"GC: Wait For Completion <cause>\"` (`L3730`), `\"HomogeneousSpaceCompact\"` (`L3954`), `\"PureTimeGcTrigger\"` (`L4327`).\n\n### 1.4 Blocking GC, Native GC Triggering & Time-Based GC\n* **Blocking GC Accounting** (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:3022-3028, 3707-3751`):\n  * `Heap::WaitForGcToComplete` -> `WaitForGcToCompleteLocked`: sets `running_collection_is_blocking_ = true` whenever a non-`HeapTaskDaemon` thread waits (`!task_processor_->IsRunningThread(self)`), accumulates `total_wait_time_`, and in `Heap::FinishGC` increments `blocking_gc_count_`, `blocking_gc_time_`, and `blocking_gc_count_last_window_`.\n* **Native GC Triggering** (`runtime/native_gc_triggering.md:1-109`, `runtime/gc/heap.h:179-190, 1301-1305, 1526-1536, 1663`, `runtime/gc/heap.cc:2757-2795, 4392-4501`):\n  * Total tracked native memory: `Heap::GetNativeBytes()` (`heap.cc:2757-2795`) = `mallinfo().uordblks + native_bytes_registered_`.\n  * Entry points from `libcore.util.NativeAllocationRegistry`:\n    1. `Heap::NotifyNativeAllocations(JNIEnv*)` (`heap.cc:4468-4471`): called once every `kNotifyNativeInterval = 64` (`heap.h:182`) malloc-backed allocations; calls `CheckGCForNative`.\n    2. `Heap::RegisterNativeAllocation(JNIEnv*, size_t bytes)` (`heap.cc:4476-4488`): non-malloc native memory; atomically adds `bytes` to `native_bytes_registered_`, increments `native_objects_notified_`, calls `CheckGCForNative` every `64` registrations OR immediately if `bytes > kCheckImmediatelyThreshold` (`10,000,000 / 64 = 156,250` bytes, `heap.h:189`), and reports `ReportAllocationForJavaHeapProf(nullptr, bytes)` (`L4487`).\n  * Watermark & Urgency (`Heap::NativeMemoryOverTarget`, `heap.cc:4403-4428`):\n    * `NativeAllocationGcWatermark() = target_footprint_ / 8 + max_free_` (`heap.h:1301-1305`).\n    * `gc_urgency = (GetBytesAllocated() + new_native_bytes / 2 + old_native_bytes / 65536) / (java_gc_start_bytes + (NativeAllocationGcWatermark() * HeapGrowthMultiplier()) / 2)`.\n  * Trigger & Blocking Throttle (`Heap::CheckGCForNative`, `heap.cc:4430-4465`):\n    * If `gc_urgency >= 1.0`, triggers concurrent full GC (`kGcCauseForNativeAlloc`, `force_full = true`).\n    * If `gc_urgency > kStopForNativeFactor` (`4.0`, `heap.cc:4398`) AND `current_native_bytes > stop_for_native_allocs_` (`-XX:StopForNativeAllocs=_`, default `1 GB` in `runtime_options.def:61`), blocks the allocating thread in a loop up to `kGcWaitIters = 20` iterations (`usleep(2000)` + `WaitForGcToComplete(kGcCauseForNativeAlloc, self)`), logging `LOG(WARNING) << \"Slept \" << i << \" times in native allocation, waiting for GC\"` every 10 iterations (`L4454-4456`).\n* **Time-Based GC Trigger** (`heap.h:174-177`, `heap-inl.h:467-497`, `heap.cc:4300-4383`):\n  * Options: `-XX:EnableTimeBasedGcTrigger=_` (`dalvik.vm.enable_time_based_gc_trigger`), `-XX:HeapMemoryGcCostFactor=_` (`dalvik.vm.heap-memory-gc-cost-factor`). Triggers concurrent GC (`ScopedTrace(\"PureTimeGcTrigger\")`) when `allocated_kb_since_last_gc * ms_since_last_gc >= time_based_gc_threshold_`.\n\n### 1.5 OutOfMemoryError Diagnostics & Heap Listeners\n* **Pre-OOME Reclamation Escalation (`Heap::AllocateInternalWithGc`)** (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:1959-2162`):\n  * Boosts allocating thread priority via `ScopedPriorityChange::SetToNormalOrBetter()` (`L2039-2040`).\n  * Escalates through `next_gc_type_` -> full GC -> clearing SoftReferences (`clear_soft_references = true`) up to `kMaxGcAttempts = 5` (`heap.cc:2025, 2088-2124`), incrementing `pre_oome_gc_count_` (`L2095`).\n  * Optionally runs `PerformHomogeneousSpaceCompact()` (`-XX:EnableHSpaceCompactForOOM`, throttled by `-XX:HSpaceCompactForOOMMinIntervalsMs`, default `100,000` ms, `runtime_options.def:85-86`), giving up early if free heap `< 1%` (`kMinFreeHeapAfterGcForAlloc = 0.01`) and newly reclaimed `< 5%` (`kMinFreedHeapAfterGcForAlloc = 0.05`, `heap.cc:186-190`).\n* **`Heap::ThrowOutOfMemoryError`** (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:1522-1576`):\n  1. Returns pre-allocated OOME if handling native stack overflow (`L1527-1531`; pre-allocated OOMEs initialized at `runtime/runtime.cc:1448-1480`).\n  2. Invokes `Runtime::Current()->OutOfMemoryErrorHook()` (`L1533`) -> triggers `perfetto_hprof::DumpPerfettoOutOfMemory`!\n  3. Builds diagnostic string (`L1537-1573`): `\"Failed to allocate a <byte_count> byte allocation with <total_bytes_free> free bytes and <FreeMemoryUntilOOME> until OOM, target footprint <target_footprint_>, growth limit <growth_limit_>\"`, plus per-space fragmentation details (`space->LogFragmentationAllocFailure`) or `\"; giving up on allocation because <1% of heap free after GC.\"` if `total_bytes_free >= byte_count`.\n* **`AllocationListener`** (`runtime/gc/allocation_listener.h:40-66`, `heap.h:975-979, 1797`, `heap.cc:1977-1982, 4695-4709`, `heap-inl.h:70-77, 229-234`):\n  * Hooks: `HasPreAlloc()`, `PreObjectAllocated(Thread*, MutableHandle<Class>, size_t*)` (can mutate class/size pre-alloc), `ObjectAllocated(Thread*, ObjPtr<Object>*, size_t)`.\n  * `SetAllocationListener` / `RemoveAllocationListener` toggle `Instrumentation::InstrumentQuickAllocEntryPoints()` so all allocations take the `kInstrumented = true` slow path (used by JVMTI).\n* **`GcPauseListener`** (`runtime/gc/gc_pause_listener.h:25-31`, `heap.h:981-989, 1799`, `heap.cc:4711-4717`, `garbage_collector.cc:427-449`):\n  * Hooks: `StartPause()`, `EndPause()`. Fired automatically by `GarbageCollector::ScopedPause` (`garbage_collector.cc:431-447`) and thread-flip root suspension (`ThreadList::FlipThreadRoots` / `SuspendAllForThreadFlip` in `concurrent_copying.cc:765` and `mark_compact.cc:906`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Heap Profiling, Leak Monitoring & Reference Processing Jank\n\n### 2.1 Perfetto Java Heap Graph & OOM Heap Dump (`perfetto_hprof`)\n* **Files**: `perfetto_hprof/perfetto_hprof.h:1-43`, `perfetto_hprof/perfetto_hprof.cc:1-1394`.\n* **Initialization & Eligibility** (`runtime/runtime.cc:1309-1318, 1600`, `AndroidRuntime.cpp:839-840`):\n  * Enabled by `-XX:PerfettoHprof=true` (`dalvik.vm.perfetto_hprof`, default `\"true\"`). Loaded in `Runtime::Start()` (`libperfetto_hprof.so`) if `Dbg::IsJdwpAllowed()` (userdebug/eng), debuggable, profileable, or `system_server`.\n* **Signal & Double-Fork Mechanics for Live Heap Dumps (`android.java_hprof`)**:\n  * `ArtPlugin_Initialize()` (`perfetto_hprof.cc:1271-1361`) creates `g_signal_pipe_fds`, registers `sigaction` for **`kJavaHeapprofdSignal = __SIGRTMIN + 6`** (`L74, 1290-1306`, capturing `si_value.sival_int` session ID and writing `'x'` to the pipe), and spawns daemon thread `\"perfetto_hprof_listener\"` (`L1308-1356`).\n  * `DumpPerfetto(Thread*)` (`L1171-1200`) -> `ForkAndRun(self, ResumeParentPolicy::IMMEDIATELY, ...)` (`L1059-1119`):\n    * Acquires `ScopedGCCriticalSection(self, kGcCauseHprof, kCollectorTypeHprof)` + `ScopedSuspendAll(__FUNCTION__, /*long_suspend=*/true)` and forks under `Locks::thread_list_lock_`.\n    * **Minimal App Pause**: Parent immediately releases `ScopedSuspendAll` and `ScopedGCCriticalSection` (`ResumeParentPolicy::IMMEDIATELY`, `L1092-1097`) and waits (`BusyWaitpid`, 1000 ms) for the first child, which immediately calls `daemon(0, 0)` (`L1187`) to double-fork a grandchild and `_exit`.\n    * **Grandchild Dump** (`WriteHeapPackets`, `L1121-1169`, `HeapGraphDumper::Dump`, `L651-1019`): arms a **120 s `SIGKILL` watchdog** (`ArmWatchdogOrDie`, `kWatchdogTimeoutSec = 120`, `L75, 111-131`), connects Perfetto data source `\"android.java_hprof\"`, optionally dumps `/proc/self/smaps` (`DumpSmaps`, `L547-567`), walks GC roots and objects (`VisitObjectsPaused`), splits `HeapGraph` protobuf packets at **`kPacketSizeThreshold = 400,000` bytes** (`L80`, fitting DropBox's 500 KB limit), captures `libcore.util.NativeAllocationRegistry.size` (`L976-982`) and space location (`HEAP_TYPE_APP`, `HEAP_TYPE_ZYGOTE`, `HEAP_TYPE_BOOT_IMAGE`), flushes, and calls `FastExit(0)`.\n* **OutOfMemoryError Heap Dump (`android.java_hprof.oom`)** (`perfetto_hprof.cc:1202-1268, 1358`):\n  * Registered via `Runtime::SetOutOfMemoryErrorHook(perfetto_hprof::DumpPerfettoOutOfMemory)` (`L1358`).\n  * Fast bailout: reads sysprop **`traced.oome_heap_session.count`** (`L1210-1214`); returns immediately if `0`. Enforces single execution per process via `g_oome_triggered` (`L1218-1223`).\n  * Uses **`ResumeParentPolicy::DEFERRED`** (`L1228-1246`): parent stays suspended in `BusyWaitpid(child, 120000)` (up to **120 s**) until the child finishes dumping, preventing the crashing app from dying early and causing `lmkd`/system_server to `SIGKILL` the process cgroup mid-dump.\n  * Child (`\"perfetto_oome_hprof\"`, no `daemon()`) registers data source **`\"android.java_hprof.oom\"`** (`L1252`), activates Perfetto trigger **`\"com.android.telemetry.art-outofmemory\"`** (`timeout_ms = 1000`, `L1253`), waits up to `1000 ms` (`TimedWaitForDataSource`, `L1258`) for a matching session (`IsOomeHeapDumpAllowed`, `L173-184` + `process_cmdline` `fnmatch`, `L285-299`), writes `HeapGraph` packets, and exits.\n\n### 2.2 Perfetto `heapprofd` Java Allocation Sampling (`HeapSampler`)\n* **Files**: `runtime/javaheapprof/javaheapsampler.h:1-98`, `runtime/javaheapprof/javaheapsampler.cc:1-85`, `runtime/gc/heap.cc:120-141, 809-812, 4614-4635, 4734-4823`.\n* **Configuration**: `-XX:PerfettoJavaHeapStackProf=true` (`dalvik.vm.perfetto_javaheap`, default `\"true\"` in `AndroidRuntime.cpp:843-844`).\n* **Registration**: `Heap::InitPerfettoJavaHeapProf()` (`heap.cc:4614-4635`) registers **`\"com.android.art\"`** via `AHeapInfo_create(\"com.android.art\")` + `AHeapProfile_registerHeap`, wiring `EnableHeapSamplerCallback` / `DisableHeapSamplerCallback`.\n* **TLAB-Shrinking Sampling Algorithm**:\n  * Default `p_sampling_interval_` = **`4096` bytes** (`4 KB`, `javaheapsampler.h:86`), dynamically updated from `AHeapProfileEnableCallbackInfo_getSamplingInterval`.\n  * Because TLAB fast-path allocations bypass C++, `HeapSampler::NextRandomTlabSize` (`javaheapsampler.cc:28-47`) caps TLAB refill target to `min(target, sampling_interval / 8)` and samples from `std::exponential_distribution<double>(1.0 / target)` under `rng_lock_`.\n  * On TLAB refill (`Heap::AllocWithNewTLAB`, `heap.cc:4820-4823` -> `ReportTlabAllocation`, `javaheapsampler.cc:57-72`), computes `adjusted_size = allocation_size + tlab_unsampled_bytes_ - pre_tlab_size`, saves `post_tlab_size` into `thread_local size_t tlab_unsampled_bytes_`, and calls `AHeapProfile_reportAllocation(perfetto_heap_id_, obj_id, adjusted_size)`.\n  * Direct non-TLAB reporting (`Heap::ReportAllocationForJavaHeapProf`, `heap-inl.h:505-509`): called on `AllocNonMovableObject` (`heap.h:290`), `AllocLargeObject` (`heap-inl.h:286`), Region non-TLAB fallback (`heap.cc:4781, 4792, 4805`), and `RegisterNativeAllocation(nullptr, bytes)` (`heap.cc:4487`). (Allocations only; frees are not reported to `heapprofd`.)\n\n### 2.3 Legacy Allocation Tracker & Standard HPROF Dumper\n* **`AllocRecordObjectMap`** (`runtime/gc/allocation_record.h:202-306`, `runtime/gc/allocation_record.cc:34-272`):\n  * Backing store for DDMS / `VMDebug.startAllocCounting` / legacy allocation tracking.\n  * Defaults: `kDefaultNumAllocRecords = 512 * 1024` (`524,288`), `kDefaultNumRecentRecords = 64 * 1024 - 1` (`65,535`), `kDefaultAllocStackDepth = 16` (configurable up to `kMaxSupportedStackDepth = 128`, `scratch.trace_depth` sysprop or DDMS).\n  * `SetAllocTrackingEnabled` (`allocation_record.cc:157-200`) instruments quick alloc entry points (`heap-inl.h:223-228`). `RecordAllocation` (`L202-264`) walks frames (`StackVisitor::WalkStack` with `kIncludeInlinedFrames`) outside `alloc_tracker_lock_` and appends `(GcRoot<Object>, AllocRecord)`. Swept during GC via `SweepAllocationRecords` (`L109-140`).\n* **Standard `hprof::DumpHeap`** (`runtime/hprof/hprof.h:27`, `runtime/hprof/hprof.cc:430-911, 1616-1627`):\n  * Implements `Debug.dumpHprofData` (`JAVA PROFILE 1.0.3` binary format) to file (`DumpToFile`, `L754-803`) or DDMS `HPDS` chunk (`DumpToDdmsDirect`, `L805-826`).\n  * Unlike `perfetto_hprof`, runs **synchronously in-process** under `ScopedGCCriticalSection` + `ScopedSuspendAll(..., /*long_suspend=*/true)` (`L1619-1622`) across two full heap passes. If `IsAllocTrackingEnabled()`, `PopulateAllocationTrackingTraces()` (`L828-866`) embeds `HPROF_TAG_STACK_TRACE` serials into every dumped object record.\n\n### 2.4 Reference Processing Contention & Jank Monitoring\n* **Files**: `runtime/gc/reference_processor.h:1-134`, `runtime/gc/reference_processor.cc:1-452`, `runtime/reference_processing_jank.md:1-84`.\n* **Mutator Blocking & Jank Detection (`ReferenceProcessor::GetReferent`)** (`reference_processor.cc:92-166`):\n  * Concurrent `RpState` progresses `kStarting` -> `kInitMarkingDone` -> `kInitClearingDone` (`reference_processor.h:111`, `reference_processor.cc:197, 222, 243`). Once `kInitMarkingDone` is reached, normal `SoftReference`/`WeakReference.get()` returns non-blocking by checking `collector_->IsMarked(referent)` (`L149-160`).\n  * Must block on `condition_.WaitHoldingLocks(self)` under `Locks::reference_processor_lock_` when `rp_state_ == kStarting`, or `reference->IsFinalizerReferenceInstance()`, or (under non-Baker RB) `PhantomReference` (`L124-139`).\n  * **Observability**:\n    * Emits ATrace slice **`\"GetReferent blocked\"`** (`ATraceBegin` at `L133`, `ATraceEnd` at `L111`).\n    * Logs jank warning if total wait exceeds **`kReportMillis = 10` ms** (`L113-116`):\n      `LOG(WARNING) << \"Weak pointer dereference blocked for \" << millis << \" milliseconds.\"`\n  * Collector-side slices: `\"Marking for <N> SoftReferences\"` (`L180-181`) and `\"Marking from <enqueued> / <total> finalizers\"` (`L261-263`).\n* **Architectural Root Cause (`runtime/reference_processing_jank.md:1-84`)**:\n  * Documents why `FinalizerReference` processing causes mutator jank: finalizer-reachable objects require a 2nd marking pass to resurrect unmarked referents, during which native weak references (`JNI WeakGlobalRef`, `InternTable` strings — governed by `Thread::GetWeakRefAccessEnabled()`) must block mutators completely because returning `nullptr` (if later resurrected) or returning an un-forwarded/un-traced pointer is unsafe.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Lock Contention, Monitor Timeout & Thread Priority Monitoring\n\n### 3.1 Thin-Lock Spinning & Inflation (`Monitor`)\n* **Files**: `runtime/monitor.h:63`, `runtime/monitor.cc:63, 1059-1197`, `runtime/runtime_options.def:151`.\n* Before inflating a thin lock, `Monitor::Lock` spins `kExtraSpinIters = 100` tight loop iterations (`monitor.cc:63, 1138`) followed by `max_spins_before_thin_lock_inflation_` (`-XX:MaxSpinsBeforeThinLockInflation=_`, default **`50`**, `monitor.h:63`) `sched_yield()` iterations (`L1153-1162`), then suspends the owner (`ThreadState::kWaitingForLockInflation`) and inflates to a fat `Monitor` (`InflateThinLocked`, `L1059-1092`).\n\n### 3.2 Fat-Lock Contention Sampling, Thresholds & Owner Tracking\n* **Configuration & Thresholds** (`runtime/monitor.cc:53-54, 84-95`, `runtime/parsed_options.cc:348-353`, `runtime/runtime_options.def:125-126`, `AndroidRuntime.cpp:267, 991-993`):\n  * `-Xlockprofthreshold:<ms>` (`Opt::LockProfThreshold`, default `0` in ART; mapped from sysprop **`dalvik.vm.lockprof.threshold`** in `AndroidRuntime.cpp:991-993`, commonly set to `500` ms on Android builds) -> `lock_profiling_threshold_`.\n  * `-Xstackdumplockprofthreshold:<ms>` (`Opt::StackDumpLockProfThreshold`, default `0`; settable via `dalvik.vm.extra-opts`) -> `stack_dump_lock_profiling_threshold_`.\n  * `kLongWaitMs = 100 * kDebugThresholdFudgeFactor` (**100 ms** in release builds, `1000 ms` in debug builds, `monitor.cc:53-54`). Both thresholds above are also multiplied by `kDebugThresholdFudgeFactor`.\n* **Owner Method & Dex PC Tracking** (`runtime/monitor.h:360-429`, `runtime/monitor-inl.h:33-81`, `runtime/monitor.cc:172-225, 507-508, 751, 854`):\n  * Uses lock-free XOR-checksummed fields (`lock_owner_`, `lock_owner_method_`, `lock_owner_dex_pc_`, `lock_owner_sum_`).\n  * **Eager** when `ATraceEnabled()`: owner records acquisition frame (`SetLockingMethod` / `SetLockingMethodNoProxy`) on `Install`/`TryLock`/`Lock`.\n  * **Lazy** when only `lock_profiling_threshold_ != 0`: contender writes `orig_owner` into `lock_owner_request_` before blocking (`monitor.cc:507-508`); owner records its release/wait site in `Unlock`/`Wait` via `CheckLockOwnerRequest` (`monitor-inl.h:33-41`).\n* **Proportional Sampling & Reporting Channels** (`Monitor::Lock`, `monitor.cc:458-636`, `Monitor::LogContentionEvent`, `runtime/monitor_android.cc:35-120`):\n  * Contender transitions to `ThreadState::kBlocked` (`L517`) and blocks on `monitor_lock_.ExclusiveLock(self)` (`L520`).\n  * **Sampling formula** (`monitor.cc:529-535`):\n    * `wait_ms >= lock_profiling_threshold_` -> `sample_percent = 100`.\n    * `wait_ms < lock_profiling_threshold_` -> `sample_percent = 100 * wait_ms / lock_profiling_threshold_`.\n    * Triggered when `sample_percent != 0 && (rand() % 100) < sample_percent`.\n  * **Reporting Channel 1 — Logcat `LOG(WARNING)`** (`monitor.cc:541-614`):\n    * If `stack_dump_lock_profiling_threshold_ > 0 && wait_ms > stack_dump_lock_profiling_threshold_`: runs synchronous checkpoint `orig_owner->RequestSynchronousCheckpoint(&owner_trace)` + `self->DumpJavaStack` and logs `\"Long monitor contention with owner <name> (<tid>) at <owner_method>(<file>:<line>) waiters=<N> in <contender_method> for <duration>\\nCurrent owner stack:\\n...\\nContender stack:\\n...\"`.\n    * Else if `wait_ms > kLongWaitMs` (**100 ms**) and `owners_method != nullptr`: logs the single-line `\"Long monitor contention with owner ...\"` warning.\n  * **Reporting Channel 2 — Binary EventLog `dvm_lock_sample` (Tag `20003`)** (`runtime/monitor_android.cc:50-109`):\n    * Writes 11 fields to `LOG_ID_EVENTS`: `[process_name (<=32 chars from /proc/self/cmdline), is_sensitive_thread (1/0 via Thread::IsSensitiveThread() -> AndroidRuntime runtime_isSensitiveThread), thread_name, wait_ms, contender_file, contender_line, contender_method, owner_file (\"-\" if identical to contender_file), owner_line, owner_method, sample_percent]`.\n  * **Reporting Channel 3 — `PaletteReportLockContention`** (`runtime/monitor_android.cc:110-119`):\n    * Invokes `PaletteReportLockContention(env, wait_ms, filename, line_number, method_name, owner_filename, owner_line_number, owner_method_name, proc_name, thread_name)` via `libartpalette` (`art/libartpalette/apex/palette.cc:225-242`).\n  * **Reporting Channel 4 — ATrace / Systrace Lock Slices**:\n    1. **Java Monitor Contention** (`monitor.cc:469-496, 634-636`, whenever `ATraceEnabled()`): `\"monitor contention with owner <name> (<tid>) at <owner_method>(<file>:<line>) waiters=<N> blocking from <contender_method>(<file>:<line>)\"`.\n    2. **Verbose Monitor Lock/Wait** (`monitor.cc:334-400`, requires BOTH `-verbose:systrace-locks` and `ATraceEnabled()`): `\"Locking <addr> at <file>:<line>\"` and `\"Waiting on <addr> at <file>:<line>\"`.\n    3. **ART Internal `BaseMutex` Contention** (`runtime/base/mutex.cc:170-190`, `ScopedContentionRecorder` whenever `ATraceEnabled()`): `\"Lock contention on <mutex_name> (owner tid: <tid>)\"`.\n\n### 3.3 In-Flight Monitor Timeout Stack Dumper (`MonitorTimeoutEnable` / `PerfMonitor`)\n* **Files**: `runtime/monitor.h:65-69, 431`, `runtime/monitor.cc:121-125, 154-158, 1774-1781`, `runtime/base/mutex.h:231-241`, `runtime/base/mutex.cc:42-60, 481-590`, `runtime/runtime.cc:1716-1727`, `runtime/runtime_options.def:76-77`, `runtime/parsed_options.cc:415-421`.\n* **Purpose**: Standard `Monitor::Lock` contention logging only fires *after* the lock is finally acquired (missing deadlocks or multi-second stalls until release). `MonitorTimeoutEnable` uses timed `futex(FUTEX_WAIT_PRIVATE)` calls to dump the owner's stack **while the contender is still blocked**.\n* **Configuration & Activation**:\n  * Options: `-XX:MonitorTimeoutEnable=<bool>` (default `false`), `-XX:MonitorTimeout=<ms>` (default **`500` ms**, clamped to **`[200, 999]` ms** in `runtime.cc:1718-1725`).\n  * `Monitor::MaybeEnableTimeout()` (`monitor.cc:1774-1781`): enables `monitor_lock_.setEnableMonitorTimeout()` if the process package is **`\"android\"`** (`system_server`) OR sysprop **`debug.art.monitor.app`** is `true`.\n* **Mechanics (`Mutex::ExclusiveLock` & `Mutex::DumpStack`)** (`runtime/base/mutex.cc:481-575`):\n  * On `ETIMEDOUT`, increments `try_times` and (for `try_times <= kMonitorTimeoutTryMax` [**5**]) calls `Mutex::DumpStack(self, wait_start_ms, try_times)`.\n  * Per-owner rate limit (`Mutex::IsDumpFrequent`, `L513-532`): stores `\"LastDumpStackTime\"` in owner's custom TLS; suppresses dump if elapsed `< kIntervalMillis * try_times` (`50 ms * try_times`).\n  * Runs synchronous checkpoint on owne